        "quiz_title": "Prilepko Mathematics Topic Question Bank",
        "class_level": "Class 12",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "For \\(x>0\\) and \\(x\\ne 1\\), if \\(\\log _2 x+\\log _x 2=\\frac{5}{2}\\), find the sum of all possible values of \\(x\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Let \\(t=\\log _2x\\). Since \\(\\log _x2=\\frac1t\\), \\(t+\\frac1t=\\frac52\\), so \\(2t^2-5t+2=0\\). Thus \\(t=2,\\frac12\\), giving \\(x=4,\\sqrt2\\). Therefore, the required sum is \\(4+\\sqrt2\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 41,
        "question_data": {
          "_meta": {
            "subject": "Mathematics",
