        "class_level": "Class 12",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "If \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are positive real numbers satisfying \\(xy=8\\) and \\(\\log _x y+\\log _y x=\\frac52\\), find \\(x+y\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Put \\(t=\\log _x y\\). Then \\(\\log _y x=\\frac1t\\), so \\(t+\\frac1t=\\frac52\\), yielding \\(t=2\\) or \\(t=\\frac12\\). Hence \\(y=x^2\\) or \\(x=y^2\\). Together with \\(xy=8\\), this gives \\((x,y)=(2,4)\\) or \\((4,2)\\). Therefore, \\(x+y=6\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 42,
        "question_data": {
          "_meta": {
            "subject": "Mathematics",
