        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "Solve the inequality \\(\\log _5(2x-1)>\\log _5(5-x)\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Both logarithms require \\(2x-1>0\\) and \\(5-x>0\\), so \\(\\frac12<x<5\\). Because the base \\(5\\) is greater than \\(1\\), \\(\\log _5(2x-1)>\\log _5(5-x)\\) is equivalent to \\(2x-1>5-x\\). Thus \\(x>2\\), and the solution is \\(\\left(2,5\\right)\\).",
