        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "Find the area of the region satisfying \\(y-2<\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\) and \\(y>2\\lvert x\\rvert\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The region lies between \\(y=2\\lvert x\\rvert\\) and \\(y=2+\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\), with \\(-1<x<1\\). Hence its area is \\(\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(2+\\sqrt{1-x^2}-2\\lvert x\\rvert\\right)dx\\). Using \\(\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\,dx=\\frac\\pi2\\) and \\(\\int_{-1}^{1}2\\lvert x\\rvert\\,dx=2\\), the area is \\(2+\\frac\\pi2\\).",
